plan Diagnostics
title   Actionable failures and safe diagnostics
status  proposed
goal
    App authors can identify a failed boundary, correct its cause and inspect all failures
    without parsing prose or leaking private data through diagnostics.
outcomes
    O1  FlowError and Diagnostic
        Expected invalid authoring throws FlowError. Owned Effects report understood expected
        failures as FlowError in the typed error channel, preserving their success and service
        requirement types. Defects and interruption remain distinct Effect outcomes.

        FlowError extends Error and exposes readonly _tag: "FlowError", code, diagnostics,
        optional cause and optional evidence. diagnostics is a nonempty readonly array; code
        equals diagnostics[0].code. The first diagnostic identifies the primary boundary failure;
        later diagnostics retain phase order and multiplicity.

        Diagnostic is an Error that authors can yield directly in Effect and encode/decode with
        its exported Schema. It exposes classification (Failure, Defect or Interruption), code,
        path (strings or finite numbers), details (string keys with string, finite number, boolean
        or null values), summary and help. Invalid tags, missing fields, unknown codes and values
        outside these domains reject. Authors branch on _tag, code, classification, path and
        details; summary and help may change without changing the failure's meaning. Decoding also
        rejects unknown values of closed details.reason fields; all serialized diagnostics use the
        same exported Schema.

        Schema rejection reports SchemaValidation with actual issue paths and safe details, unless
        the owning boundary defines a more specific code. Parser exceptions never escape as raw
        exceptions; arbitrary callback defects are never mislabeled SchemaValidation. Story failure
        evidence follows @plan.Testing.O8.

        Diagnostics are not endings. A call's ending is a value the machine maps
        (@plan.Operations.O3): Flow's reasons NotSent { why } and the unknowns are reserved tags,
        and the evidence kinds Superseded, Released, NothingToResend and InFlight are records, not
        diagnostic codes. Denial codes are check() data, not diagnostic codes: InvalidTurn and
        NotInState (@plan.Machines.O4), LateMayNotLeave (@plan.Machines.O6), InFlight, Uncertain,
        RetryLimit and NothingToResend (an operation's idle and retryable guards,
        @plan.Operations.O3), and Unencodable (a guard key with no form, @plan.Operations.O3);
        NothingToResend and InFlight name both a guard denial and an evidence record.
    O2  Recognizable codes and corrective action
        Codes identify failures independently of message wording. Each diagnostic names the
        affected field, identity or bound in path/details and gives a concrete corrective action in
        help. Reporting an issue does not itself mean the call rejects; the owning boundary decides
        whether work fails, continues or falls back. Application guard deny codes remain
        application data, separate from Flow's diagnostic vocabulary. A specific boundary code
        takes precedence over a generic machine-configuration code when both describe the same
        violation.

        Classification defaults to Failure. InvariantViolation, Defect, GuardDefect,
        EntryMismatch, ServerOnlyImport, HydrateOutsideProvider and HydrationCrossRequest classify
        as Defect; Interruption classifies as Interruption. A failure during lazy adoption keeps
        the code and classification it would have at App construction. Warning or informational
        severity never changes classification.

        The vocabulary is closed: a code outside this list is a defect in Flow. Each line gives
        the owner and the corrective action an author takes. Names the user has not confirmed are
        marked proposed, as their owner plans mark them.

        General
        - SchemaValidation: correct the value at the reported Schema issue path.
        - InvalidConfiguration (@plan.Machines.O1, @plan.Runtime.O1, @plan.Operations.O1,
        @plan.LazyFeatures.O2, @plan.Package.O3, @plan.EntityDomains.O1): fix the declaration
        named by path; details.reason names the rule, such as a duplicate id or an undeclared
        patch entity.
        - InvariantViolation: report a Flow bug; the Runtime stopped to protect state.
        - Defect and GuardDefect (@plan.Machines.O3, @plan.Machines.O4): fix the failing callback
        or service using the in-process cause.
        - Interruption: honor cleanup; retry only while the original intent still holds.
        - CleanupFailed (@plan.Runtime.O6): repair the finalizer and replace the owning Runtime.
        - UnencodableValue (@plan.Operations.O3, @plan.Persistence.O5): replace the Symbol,
        function, Map or Set with a value that has an encoded form.

        Definitions and fragments (construction errors and flow check findings)
        - TwoDefaults, ImpureDefault (proposed), IdentityFieldOptional (proposed),
        ReservedStateName, UnknownNotUncertain (@plan.Machines.O1): keep one pure default per
        field; make a value-named machine's input fields required and default-free; rename the
        state; target a Flow.uncertain event or Flow.ignore.
        - RestoreMissingInput (@plan.Machines.O1, @plan.Persistence.O5): give the new input field
        a default, or expect the record to be quarantined.
        - InputFieldForm (@plan.CommandLine.O5): use an input field whose decoded form can be
        carried.
        - ScheduleLeadsToWrite (@plan.CommandLine.O5): persist the machine, commit on close, lift
        the actor's use, or give the write a precondition.
        - AsksForever (@plan.CommandLine.O5): give the handler a path that does not ask again.

        Runtime and actors
        - RuntimeNotReady, RuntimeDisposed (@plan.Runtime.O2, @plan.Runtime.O6): await ready();
        create a new Runtime after disposal.
        - IdentityExhausted (@plan.Runtime.C2): replace the Runtime.
        - ConflictingActorRef (@plan.Runtime.O3): give refs of one identity the same context.
        - ForeignActorRef (@plan.React.O2): use handles and refs from this Runtime's App.
        - MissingContextProvider, ContextCycle (@plan.Runtime.O5): wire every slot to an acyclic
        upward provider.
        - BlockedByDependents (@plan.Runtime.O6): dispose the named consumers first.
        - InvalidEvent, AdmissionOverloaded, SendTargetAbsent (@plan.Runtime.O4): send a valid
        public event; wait or shrink the batch; ensure the target before sending
        (details.reason: NoRecord, RecordUndecodable or NotAdopted).
        - RecordUndecodable (proposed) (@plan.Runtime.O3): expected after an incompatible release;
        an ensure starts fresh.
        - EndedWithWork (development warning, @plan.Runtime.O3): lift the actor's use, or move the
        work into the screen's state.
        - TurnStorm (evidence, @plan.Runtime.O4): add a backoff on an explicit retry with a delay.

        Operations and entity domains
        - InvalidKey (@plan.Operations.O1): fix the key value at the reported path.
        - InvalidWrite (@plan.Operations.O3): make the success write match the target Schema.
        - SharedContract (proposed), DuplicatePlacement, VerbMismatch, KeyRequired, UnresolvedHold,
        KeyOmitsInput, KeyFieldOptional, UnusedOperation, ReservedReason (proposed),
        PreviousIsCurrent (proposed) (@plan.Operations.O1, @plan.Operations.O3,
        @plan.CommandLine.O5): fix the declaration named; give every hold an owner.
        - OldVersionLane (@plan.Operations.O3, @plan.Persistence.O5): ship handlers through
        previous[i] for the old key's holds.
        - DuplicateSession, FeedUnhandled, ListenNeedsEvery, DuplicateListen, SharedFills,
        FillsNotPerKey, UnboundedBridge (@plan.Operations.O4, @plan.CommandLine.O5): one session
        per operation and key; map every required stream key; name a field only one operation
        fills. SelectedNoKey (proposed, @plan.Operations.O4) is an issue; Feed's reasons (Closed,
        Overflow, Silent, Flapping) and missed's (Unproven, Lost, Reset) are ending values, not
        codes.
        - Stream session flags, diagnostic records that decide nothing (@plan.Inspection.O1,
        @plan.Runtime.O6 for release): ValuesWhileDown, RegistrationChurn, ReleaseOverdue,
        ProofWithoutPosition, PingsWithoutLive, IdleWithoutPing (proposed), DeliveryDenied,
        FillsUntouched, FillsOtherKey (proposed): read the session's facts; fix the adapter's
        signals, the fills field or the release.
        - UserClosure (@plan.Operations.O2, @plan.Operations.O4): fix the mapper or select that
        threw or returned no shape.
        - HiddenOrder, HiddenFilter, UndeclaredEffect (@plan.EntityDomains.O1,
        @plan.EntityDomains.O4): declare the missing sort key, condition or alsoChanges.
        - GoneWithoutKey, GuardedUnbound, GuardedWithoutVersion, GuardedWithoutTarget,
        PredictionNotRetained (proposed names except PredictionNotRetained;
        @plan.EntityDomains.O1, @plan.CommandLine.O5): add .byKey; declare the version and
        target; give the predicted field a carrier.
        - Stale, RecordHeld, RepairOverdue (proposed), UnsettledEvicted (proposed),
        GuardContradicted (proposed), InputDecodeFailed (evidence, @plan.EntityDomains.O1):
        expected store facts; read their causes.

        Persistence and lazy features
        - StorageFailure (@plan.Persistence.O5): restore storage availability or quota; do not
        assume the write is durable.
        - StorageSilent (evidence, @plan.Persistence.O3): the disk has not answered; nothing is
        decided.
        - NonDurableContextProvider (@plan.Persistence.O3): persist the named providers.
        - RecordShapeChanged (proposed), FieldDropped (proposed), HoldWithoutRecord (proposed),
        OldVersionActor (proposed), UnboundLane (proposed), LaneRekeyed (proposed), OpRenamed
        (proposed), LaneRekeyCollision (proposed), HoldForgotten (proposed) (@plan.Persistence.O5,
        @plan.Runtime.O6): expected after a release that changed a saved shape, field, identity or
        operation; reconcile or cancel the named holds.
        - SecondTabNoPersistence (@plan.Persistence.O7): close the other owner or continue without
        persistence.
        - EntryLoadFailed, EntryMismatch (@plan.LazyFeatures.O4, @plan.LazyFeatures.O2): fix the
        import or the declared id.

        Server rendering
        - ServerOnlyImport (@plan.Package.O1): import flow-state/server only in server code.
        - DehydratePersistentSetup (@plan.ServerRendering.O1): pass a setup without persistence.
        - DehydrateUnsettled, ConcurrentCapture (@plan.ServerRendering.O2): raise within or stream
        the slow read separately; retry the request.
        - DehydrateCommitInFlight, DehydrateTooLarge (@plan.ServerRendering.O3): commit from the
        client; split or narrow the payload.
        - HydrateOutsideProvider, HydrationCrossRequest, HydrationScopeMismatch
        (@plan.ServerRendering.O4, @plan.ServerRendering.O6): wrap in FlowProvider; construct the
        Runtime inside the provider; give both setups the same scope.
        - HydrationIncompatible, HydrationMalformed, HydrationRejected (@plan.ServerRendering.O4):
        diagnostics only; the client loads normally. A persistent one means mismatched code.

        Stories
        - StoryTurnLimit (details.reason Settle or Advance), InvalidDuration (@plan.Testing.O2):
        break the send cycle; move time forward by a finite amount.
        - HostTimeWait (@plan.Testing.O2): remove the real host wait from the run.
        - StoryInvalidCommand (details.reason ActorAbsent, AlreadyEntered, NotEntered, TabOpen,
        TabClosed, NothingHeld, NoDeadline or NoConnection), SubjectAbsent, AmbiguousRead
        (@plan.Testing.O8, @plan.Testing.O4): fix the step or the read named.
        - StoryFakeError (details.reason NoRoute, InvalidInput, Crashed, UnplacedStream or
        InvalidRefusal) (@plan.Testing.O3): fix the fake or its binding.
        - FramesTruncated, PropertyTestFailed, PropertyDefect (@plan.Testing.O4,
        @plan.Testing.O6): read checkpoints instead of every frame; shrink and fix the property.
        - DuplicateFixture (@plan.Testing.O3): use the overriding form to replace a service.
        - UnusedWireRule (@plan.Testing.O3): remove the wire rule or the step that needs it.

        Inspection, artifacts and the command line
        - CodecBoundExceeded, CodecMalformed, CodecSchemaMismatch (@plan.Inspection.O2).
        - InvalidInspectorCapacity, InspectorAlreadyAttached, InspectorSinkFailed
        (@plan.Inspection.O3).
        - InvalidTraceRecord, InvalidLifecycleTransition, InvalidStoryEvidence,
        ArtifactIdentityMismatch, InvalidArtifactOperand (@plan.Inspection.O4,
        @plan.Inspection.O6). UnknownSelector names a selector unknown to the app's Model.
        EvidenceUnavailable is not a failure: it marks an answer whose evidence was not retained,
        which reports insufficient evidence and exits 0.
        - TypeFactsUnavailable (@plan.Inspection.D2): run where complete type facts exist.
        - InvalidUsage (@plan.CommandLine.O1): fix the command, option or operand named.
        - ConfigLoadFailed (@plan.CommandLine.O6): fix flow.config.ts, the app or the revision
        named.
        - OutputFailed (@plan.CommandLine.O2): free or choose the destination; check permissions.

        Superseded: "InputIgnored (@plan.Runtime.O3): the actor already exists; its first input
        stands." is removed: no ensure takes input (C144). "ConflictingActorRef ... give refs with
        one identity the same options" now names context only (C160). "InvalidAttempt
        (@plan.Operations.O3): retry only an Attempt from this descriptor, with valid input." is
        removed with retry(attempt) (C23). "DuplicateStreamSession (@plan.Operations.O4): open one
        session per actor and key." is replaced by the DuplicateSession warning (C87; C103).
        "RestoreDiscarded (@plan.Persistence.O5): expected after a version change; otherwise
        inspect the reason (incompatible, corrupt, orphan)." is replaced by RecordUndecodable,
        RecordShapeChanged and the quarantine names (C143; C152; C211). The Story names (C83), the
        stream names (C103), ScheduleLeadsToWrite and EndedWithWork (C125), TurnStorm and
        AsksForever (C132), ReservedStateName, InputFieldForm, UnknownNotUncertain and
        UnencodableValue (C145; C154), IdentityFieldOptional (C121) and ImpureDefault (C157;
        C184) are added, with the names other plans' rows define (C18; C65; C177; C193; C209;
        C211-C215).
    O3  Complete failures survive cleanup
        An author inspecting an in-process failure can recover its complete Effect Cause when
        available, including failures from finalizers and cancellation. Cleanup never replaces the
        execution failure or erases another failure. Classification is Defect if any defect
        exists, otherwise Failure if a typed failure exists, otherwise Interruption.

        Classification does not reorder diagnostics: execution or cancellation stays primary;
        when only cleanup fails, the first cleanup failure is primary. Remaining cleanup
        diagnostics retain phase order and multiplicity, including after end capture. Operation
        failure, defect, interruption and an unknown remote ending remain distinct. Promise
        adapters and Effect's own AbortSignal preserve the complete Cause until the host
        deliberately projects the result. Complete Exit and Cause survive evidence acceptance as
        well as cleanup. A thrown exception or Promise rejection never becomes a reusable service's
        typed failure channel.

        Only the in-process FlowError may expose raw Cause. Cause, stack traces and fiber ids
        never enter snapshots, checkpoints, persistence, SSR payloads, traces, inspector events or
        CLI output. Outbound application data follows @plan.Inspection.O5; SSR omission follows
        @plan.ServerRendering.O3.

        Superseded: "forwarded AbortSignal cancellation" reads Effect's own signal: contexts carry
        no signal (C116).
    O4  Safe rendering
        Rendering a Diagnostic preserves its code, path, safe details and actionable help. Control
        characters in paths, details, summary and help are escaped so hostile names cannot inject
        terminal or log commands. Output never exposes raw input, stacks or Cause, and never
        invents a file, line or column. Locations appear only when actually known.
decisions
    D1  One public failure contract
        FlowError is the shared boundary carrier and Diagnostic its shared diagnostic Schema.
        Capability-specific error classes or competing diagnostic codecs are not public APIs.
        The one exception is the testing route's PropertyTestFailed, which carries a property
        test's result (@plan.Package.O1); Fake.Lost, Fake.Refused and Fake.Closed are a fake's
        answer values, not Flow failures.
verification
    V1  Codec and carrier tests prove @O1's fields, closed-reason rejection and primary code.
    V2  Type tests prove readonly diagnostics, yieldable Diagnostic and preserved Effect A/R.
    V3  Boundary tests prove code precedence, classifications, missing-evidence meaning and safe
        Schema paths.
    V4  Mixed-Cause tests prove complete causes, classification and ordering through cleanup.
    V5  Rendering/export tests prove safe actionable output without leaks or invented locations.
questions
    Q1  Deferred to build time
        Per-code help wording and the closed details.reason values. Diagnostic codec
        implementation. Host execution helpers and printer organization. Exact evidence
        projections and counters within the owning evidence contract.
